====Verb====
{{fr-verb}}

# {{lb|fr|literally}} to [[carry]] something back to where it was
# {{lb|fr|literally}} to [[wear]] again
# to [[transfer]] {{gloss|an emotion}}
#: {{uxi|fr|'''reporter''' son amour sur quelqu'un|'''to transfer''' one's love to somebody}}
# to [[put back]]; to [[put off]]; to [[postpone]]
#: {{ux|fr|Après avoir été '''reportées''' de nombreuses fois, les épreuves ont finalement eu lieu.|After having been '''postponed''' numerous times, the exams finally took place.}}
#* {{quote-book|fr|year=1999|author=w:Chrystine Brouillet|title=Les Fiancées de l'Enfer|isbn=2-89021-363-3|page=113|passage=''Graham avait '''reporté''' la fête, suggérant d'attendre la fin de l'enquête sur le violeur pour s'amuser.''|translation=''Graham had '''put back''' the party, suggesting to wait until the investigation about the rapist was over to have fun.''}}
# {{lb|fr|usually|impersonal}} to [[carry]] or [[take]] back in time
#: {{ux|fr|Il faut '''se reporter''' au mois dernier pour comprendre.|We have '''to go back in time''' a month to understand.}}
# {{lb|fr|pronominal}} to [[refer]]; to [[check]]
#: {{ux|fr|Pour mieux saisir le problème, on '''se reportera''' au chapitre 4.|To better understand the issue, the reader is '''referred''' to chapter 4.}}
# {{lb|fr|mathematics|and|finance}} to [[carry]] over or forward
#: {{ux|fr|Cet idiot avait oublié de '''reporter''' un 3!|That idiot forgot to '''carry over''' a 3!}}

